  "body": "The selected **complex m=73/max-rank-48** profile has exact worst-path thresholds `b_1=73`, `b_(d+1)=73*ceil(b_d/48)` under its inherited floor-child and terminal contracts. The written proof establishes the sharp asymptotic depth rate and an exact **43/26** allowance. This is a research note / scoped mathematical audit, with **no new \u03ba or supplier adoption**.\n\nThe source-bound finite stock has 2,642 bits. Replacing only its modeled depth component gives a **conditional** row comparison `16469 -> 15555` (914 less). The per-level physical divisor and other row-ledger terms still need admission; this number is not inserted into the selected receipt. All helpers, private centres, coefficient work, precision reserves and recursive children remain charged.\n\nThe ordinary bootstrap is separately **BIT m=64/max-rank-42**. Concurrent Adam Gall PR2084 and PR2087 prompted an explicit producer-boundary check, independently corroborated against the frozen PR589 record. This m=73 result does not supply their ordinary producer's stock coefficient. The selected stage-2 exponent is used only for a parameter comparison. The predecessor two-level halving guard is credited, not claimed as new.\n\nVerification on CPython 3.12.13, standard library only:\n\n- All 2,080 block decisions for `1<=p<=64, 1<=q<=p`: 1,227 pass, with 43/26 the minimum **within that domain**.\n- Forward recursion, inverse thresholds and an all-child dynamic program agree on 103,139 widths, including every width 0..100,000 and power/threshold boundaries.\n- Twelve semantic/source controls reject; eight focused tests pass normally and with `-O`; direct optimized replay, package metadata, source baseline and staged diff checks pass.\n\nReproduce:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/selected-coarse-depth-stock\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_SELECTED_COARSE_DEPTH_STOCK block=43/26 widths=103139 conditional_row=16469->15555 controls=12 no_new_kappa`, followed by passing normal/optimized tests and `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=completed`.\n\nScientific base: `564148b82ae9df72163f22106f15e73efca8aff2`; contribution `0aca64e29d43533743bb912ac8b77b434e04b84a`. Refreshed main `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2` has unchanged catalogue, selected record and all nine scientific inputs. Source/archive pins, proof, exact receipt, scope change and handoff are in `research/selected-coarse-depth-stock/`. Final overlap covered 367 open PRs and 752 Discussion records with complete pagination, followed by fresh related-head checks; this is not a novelty certificate. [Original claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18932040).\n\nAll-size lowering, physical/compiler/hosting, completed-row, precision/tape and analytic assumptions remain inherited. No full selected cold replay, formal-kernel acceptance, independent human review or hosted-CI success is claimed. Frozen predecessors, upstream/ and the selected frontier are unchanged.\n\nCredit Josie Elliston (PR1956/1965), ToikY (PR1990), Rohan Arun (PR1094/387), Jeremy Kothe (PR1087), Hao Yan (T16), the PR185/eumemic/DreamingOfClouds lineage, existing stock corroboration including PR1407, and Adam Gall's concurrent PR2084/2087. Prepared by Sricharan Vagvala (@theon199) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in research, proof, implementation, validation and writing. Apache-2.0.\n",
